From 01e0e78a7209b2637b0cc44091ff1f73cb8c8740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:34:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] User journey: one page, one panel, a simpler flow

Users found the user journey confusing. As head of product, the flow is
reworked around what people actually do there: look at the map, open a
moment, change it.

- One menu. Journey tags (U089) is no longer a separate page; its table,
  coverage and tag setup are tabs of User journey (Map, Tags & review,
  Coverage, Tag setup). /admin/journey-tags redirects to the tags tab.
- The map fits the page: four stage columns with no zoom and no sideways
  scroll at desktop widths. Filters are the stage chips, a tag filter and
  a Show product screens switch.
- Every card is one button. With tags on, it shows readiness, the review
  status and 'Tags missing' when the classification is incomplete.
- One side panel for everything about a moment: stage (so it can move),
  title, what happens, the potential feature, the illustration, then its
  tags, review status and note, saved with one button. The map stays in
  view beside it. Screens use the same panel without tags.
- One primary action, Add moment (with its stage chosen in the panel);
  the rest moves under More: stage names (all four at once), Export,
  Import, Restore the original.
- Export writes the map and the tags in one file; Import reads it, the
  older single exports and the original blueprint page's export.

On production (RELEASES.journeyTags off) the page is the map and the
panel without tags. Shared pieces: admin/components/SidePanel,
admin/pages/journey/TagViews, admin/data/journeyBundle (tested).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
